":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T05:33:45-08:00","id":1288578,"title":"","content":"I had someone on a discord suggest making it a martial art that begins at e3\u2014giving it a basis for \u201cthe best martial art\u201d to be sought after. I\u2019ve also considered focusing on the breathing manipulation, maybe basing it\u2019s early stages on Taoist martial arts? Building up cultivation and at the upper levels releasing it as a single point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T06:11:07-08:00","id":1288584,"title":"","content":"Honestly that still sounds like an SMA, just an unusually direct one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T07:31:05-08:00","id":1288595,"title":"","content":"The tricky thing with Ki Rata is it looks like it's basically just 'Punch, but more', which isn't usually how charms work.<br /> <br /> Until we see it doing something more than 'Punch, but more', it's a pretty straight forward combination of Excellency and 'throw every damage enhancing Charm you can on to the attack'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T11:08:58-08:00","id":1288645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1288564#post1288564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based mostly on the description.<br /> 'Points' are a special resource that are part of the charm costs that can be obtained <i>somehow</i> which makes having 1-2 of them available to you a given, but higher numbers harder to reach and potentially unsafe for the Martial Artist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my immediate thought was that it should be something like White Reaper with the Halos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:39:43-08:00","id":1288778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1288578#post1288578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had someone on a discord suggest making it a martial art that begins at e3\u2014giving it a basis for \u201cthe best martial art\u201d to be sought after. I\u2019ve also considered focusing on the breathing manipulation, maybe basing it\u2019s early stages on Taoist martial arts? Building up cultivation and at the upper levels releasing it as a single point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider maybe making it a Martial Art that uses a mechanic similar to the Stormcaller\u2019s Storm building effect, there could be a cap on points (say Essence x 2) maybe the capstone is an AOE effect with points determining rage, such that an E5 character might be able to make it out to long range? This is still hideously powerful but it could still be within the realm of possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:44:23-08:00","id":1291593,"title":"","content":"The problem is that its defining feature is &quot;the strongest martial art ever&quot;, much moreso than its actual techniques or mechanics or anything like that. That's not something that can easily be added to a tabletop game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:01:30-08:00","id":1291601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1291593#post1291593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that its defining feature is &amp;quot;the strongest martial art ever&amp;quot;, much moreso than its actual techniques or mechanics or anything like that. That's not something that can easily be added to a tabletop game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did notice it\u2019s absence from Broken World. I think I\u2019ll wait to make it until after the arc\u2014the ideas I had are either reminiscent of Prismatic Arranfsment or an art for my own projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:15:22-08:00","id":1291628,"title":"","content":"Ki Rata's whole thing is that it's incredibly dangerous because it really is just the One Weird Trick that someone figured out that makes you win at fighting, right? It's h4x. It's like regular karate, like, not much more difficult to learn than regular karate, except if you learn it instead of learning karate, you can blow up cities. Whoops! Unfortunate that reality allows for such a thing, better police the hell out of the whole cosmos to ensure nobody spreads or exploits it!<br /> <br /> This doesn't really work in any system that assumes equal XP expenditures will lead to somewhat balanced characters. Which, like, I know, I know, <i>Exalted</i>, linear BP/exponential XP, feel free to laugh. But it's still a problem. You can't make a &quot;balanced&quot; version of Ki Rata because there isn't anything to Ki Rata except how unbalanced it is. Being phenomenally, existentially imbalanced is what Ki Rata <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> (Ironically it'd be easy to do in Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine because.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T16:07:54-08:00","id":1291645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1291628#post1291628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ki Rata's whole thing is that it's incredibly dangerous because it really is just the One Weird Trick that someone figured out that makes you win at fighting, right? It's h4x. It's like regular karate, like, not much more difficult to learn than regular karate, except if you learn it instead of learning karate, you can blow up cities. Whoops! Unfortunate that reality allows for such a thing, better police the hell out of the whole cosmos to ensure nobody spreads or exploits it!<br /> <br /> This doesn't really work in any system that assumes equal XP expenditures will lead to somewhat balanced characters. Which, like, I know, I know, <i>Exalted</i>, linear BP/exponential XP, feel free to laugh. But it's still a problem. You can't make a &quot;balanced&quot; version of Ki Rata because there isn't anything to Ki Rata except how unbalanced it is. Being phenomenally, existentially imbalanced is what Ki Rata <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> (Ironically it'd be easy to do in Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine because.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Reality Syndrome 4 lyfe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T16:25:17-08:00","id":1291649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1291628#post1291628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like regular karate, like, not much more difficult to learn than regular karate, except if you learn it instead of learning karate, you can blow up cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think regular karate is something where, if you learn it wrong, you tear yourself to shreds, and the only people around to learn you it right will only do so if they're reasonably sure you'll never use it but to put down that one in a trillion person who managed to not tear themselves to shreds learning it wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:21:26-08:00","id":1291784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1291649#post1291649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think regular karate is something where, if you learn it wrong, you tear yourself to shreds</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easier than you imagine. More than one hyper studend of, say, muay thai, broke a shin or the hip because he overreached.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T06:27:09-08:00","id":1291807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1291628#post1291628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ki Rata's whole thing is that it's incredibly dangerous because it really is just the One Weird Trick that someone figured out that makes you win at fighting, right? It's h4x. It's like regular karate, like, not much more difficult to learn than regular karate, except if you learn it instead of learning karate, you can blow up cities. Whoops! Unfortunate that reality allows for such a thing, better police the hell out of the whole cosmos to ensure nobody spreads or exploits it!<br /> <br /> This doesn't really work in any system that assumes equal XP expenditures will lead to somewhat balanced characters. Which, like, I know, I know, <i>Exalted</i>, linear BP/exponential XP, feel free to laugh. But it's still a problem. You can't make a &amp;quot;balanced&amp;quot; version of Ki Rata because there isn't anything to Ki Rata except how unbalanced it is. Being phenomenally, existentially imbalanced is what Ki Rata <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> (Ironically it'd be easy to do in Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine because.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is doubly true and the other problem I ran into. Explosive punches that done wrong hurt you might work but \u201cstrongest art ever\u201d doesn\u2019t really jive with TTRPG play in exalted. <br /> <br /> I also realized that Ki Rata sounds a lot like Karate depending on how you say that last a.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T05:28:40-08:00","id":1434748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1291601#post1291601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did notice it\u2019s absence from Broken World. I think I\u2019ll wait to make it until after the arc\u2014the ideas I had are either reminiscent of Prismatic Arranfsment or an art for my own projects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well its after the arc and we have an idea of Ki Rata's signature trick being Time Stop. Any further thoughts that this has ellicited?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 02-07-2021, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T08:33:13-08:00","id":1434753,"title":"","content":"Definitely seems to be a major branch of the &quot;charm tree&quot;. <br /> <br /> Although I guess it's a more esoteric manifestation of the stated principle of focusing force at a single point. They just don't only do that in space, but also in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T11:59:48-08:00","id":1434770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434748#post1434748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> well its after the arc and we have an idea of Ki Rata's signature trick being Time Stop. Any further thoughts that this has ellicited?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is time stoppage a trait of ki rata or is it a trait of his Key?<br /> I say this for two reasons<br /> 1) We have seen it used to great effect a couple times without apparent fuckery of time. While it could mean it was omitted for future flexing on the reader, I'd put the odds at it just not being there. Summoning the key's powers during a tense meeting would surely taunt the other demiurges into an open battle, in ways that &quot;just&quot; breaking some shit with an overpowered technique wouldn't.<br /> 2) Ki Rata's always been depicted as demanding a ludicrous capacity to focus. Stopping time sure feels like one of the best ways you could summon up the time and peace of mind to concentrate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T15:05:13-08:00","id":1434786,"title":"","content":"The style has a spectrum of power between &quot;shatter tables with a poke/send decapitating waves of air with a finger flick&quot; and &quot;enough force to destroy a city&quot;, with being in a state of relative speed that all else is frozen while you obliterate it being in the middle.<br /> <br /> Abbadon has talked about Ki Rata and the comic pages in terms of &quot;yeah, this is the secret to its success&quot;, and we keep seeing him breathe in right before everything stops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T16:02:03-08:00","id":1434794,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you want a bare-fisted fighter who can tear through everything in their way with raw speed and strength... isn't that just Solar Brawl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T04:59:01-08:00","id":1434832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434794#post1434794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you want a bare-fisted fighter who can tear through everything in their way with raw speed and strength... isn't that just Solar Brawl?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Brawl doesn't let you break action economy.<br /> <br /> Ki Rata is more akin to the capstones of Mantis and Centipede styles, except risen to SMA levels, with Gnomon Evocations thrown in for good measure. Wasn't there gonna be a new Time-messing SMA in the Sidereals book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T07:26:58-08:00","id":1434845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434832#post1434832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Brawl doesn't let you break action economy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not mechanically, but charms like Rampage-Berserker Attack and Lightning Strikes Twice do a pretty solid job of representing &quot;I can hit you a hundred times in a second!&quot; Adamantine/Orichalcum Fists of Battle and Ascendant Battle Visage (and Increasing Strength Meditation) are your &quot;take a deep breath to build power,&quot; and Sledgehammer Fist Punch is almost exactly how I'd write a charm to let you shatter a stone table with your pinkie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T08:23:45-08:00","id":1434852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434845#post1434845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps not mechanically, but charms like Rampage-Berserker Attack and Lightning Strikes Twice do a pretty solid job of representing &quot;I can hit you a hundred times in a second!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not solid enough, IMO, or your hundred strikes rapidly become less potent individually than if you made one. The point of Ki Rata is that it allows you to act more than your opponent, and it's consequently broken as a result. If some combination of charm let you attack twice, that'd be a start, but it's still a far cry from the higher-end stuff Solomon David is pulling in the newer installments, where he delivers 10k punches within a single instance of timestop. I think that the point of Ki Rata, as it were, is that each such punch is exactly as if Solomon David punched you once, with the concomitant insane multiplier to total damage and such, and Exalted doesn't really support that in its combat paradigm (since that would make Ki Rata extremely broken and a MA that stands head and shoulders above all else \u2014 which is pretty much exactly what it is in KSBD.)<br /> <br /> The closest analogue to what he is doing that I can think of is actually something like Obsidian Shards of Infinity Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T11:11:22-08:00","id":1434861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434852#post1434852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not solid enough, IMO, or your hundred strikes rapidly become less potent individually than if you made one. The point of Ki Rata is that it allows you to act more than your opponent, and it's consequently broken as a result. If some combination of charm let you attack twice, that'd be a start, but it's still a far cry from the higher-end stuff Solomon David is pulling in the newer installments, where he delivers 10k punches within a single instance of timestop. I think that the point of Ki Rata, as it were, is that each such punch is exactly as if Solomon David punched you once, with the concomitant insane multiplier to total damage and such, and Exalted doesn't really support that in its combat paradigm (since that would make Ki Rata extremely broken and a MA that stands head and shoulders above all else \u2014 which is pretty much exactly what it is in KSBD.)<br /> <br /> The closest analogue to what he is doing that I can think of is actually something like Obsidian Shards of Infinity Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair... But we're also only seeing Ki Rata as performed by Solomon David--a being who, if we take the ancient demiurges to be analogous to Solars, has siezed a full seventh of all the power of the Solar host-- 40-plus Solar Exaltations jammed into his forehead. Comparing Solomon's martial arts ability to a Solar's is like the Solar's skills to a mortal's. The stuff attributed to non-god-tier practitioners-- decapitating a man with air pressure, vaporizing the bones in a foe's arms, even destroying citites--doesn't sound any crazier than what a high-Essence Dawn can do using published charms.<br /> <br /> A Ki Rata style intended for player use, then, might be something along the lines of Solar Brawl, or maybe SPSitV--stretching the action economy and delivering disgusting amounts of damage, but expensive and with defensive weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T11:50:42-08:00","id":1434867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434852#post1434852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not solid enough, IMO, or your hundred strikes rapidly become less potent individually than if you made one. The point of Ki Rata is that it allows you to act more than your opponent, and it's consequently broken as a result. If some combination of charm let you attack twice, that'd be a start, but it's still a far cry from the higher-end stuff Solomon David is pulling in the newer installments, where he delivers 10k punches within a single instance of timestop. I think that the point of Ki Rata, as it were, is that each such punch is exactly as if Solomon David punched you once, with the concomitant insane multiplier to total damage and such, and Exalted doesn't really support that in its combat paradigm (since that would make Ki Rata extremely broken and a MA that stands head and shoulders above all else \u2014 which is pretty much exactly what it is in KSBD.)<br /> <br /> The closest analogue to what he is doing that I can think of is actually something like Obsidian Shards of Infinity Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you are really looking for is the Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick. Or, more specifically, it's Grandmother Spider Mastery part.<br /> <br /> Yes. 2e SMA styles had their problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 02-08-2021, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T14:03:45-08:00","id":1434883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434867#post1434867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you are really looking for is the Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick. Or, more specifically, it's Grandmother Spider Mastery part.<br /> <br /> Yes. 2e SMA styles had their problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being permissive enough of what counted as people being in line of sight and presuming an accessible vantage point from which to view all of Creation weren't exactly mechanics problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T14:08:29-08:00","id":1434885,"title":"","content":"Yes, Brawl does not often break the action economy... but neither does Ki Rata that we have seen? Many Charms in Exalted are fluffed precisely like Ki Rata is - Solomon David's ability to just turn a group of people to blood sprays in the span of a single second may as well be represented by a charm that strikes several enemies around you and is just fluffed like you moved fast and hit them all individually (as several multi-target charms are); his duel with White Chain was mostly represented by being just plain stronger than her, not attacking her 20 times before she could react (in fact, as soon as he tried to do precisely that, she reacted at the same speed as he did.); it has a very interesting fluff, but its in-story effect is not very different from what you can actually already do with Brawl and re-fluffing certain MAs.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Exalted has several arts which are sold as Ki Rata, and in the hands of powerful Solars/Sidereals live up to the name and fluff... until they meet Another Ultimate Fighting Style, which Exalted has far more than one of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T14:56:09-08:00","id":1434886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434885#post1434885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">his duel with White Chain was mostly represented by being just plain stronger than her, not attacking her 20 times before she could react (in fact, as soon as he tried to do precisely that, she reacted at the same speed as he did.); it has a very interesting fluff, but its in-story effect is not very different from what you can actually already do with Brawl and re-fluffing certain MAs.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He explicitly spends most of the fight limiting himself to the same styles that she is using, when he actually employs Ki Rata in its lowest level it definitely comes across as hitting her twenty times before she can react, and the capacity to catch up with him when he's stopping time is clearly exceptional, unprecedented, a visible struggle in comparison and still tears her body apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T16:58:17-08:00","id":1434890,"title":"","content":"Unless Abandon has explicitly said something, I don't believe he's literally stopping time. He's just moving so fast that for all appearances it looks like time has stopped. Ki Rata has been about being so fast and strong that the opponent has no chance. I don't see it going to literally warping the fabric of spacetime is a result of the style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T18:34:17-08:00","id":1434897,"title":"","content":"I think Solomon is going super fast, but on a vibrational level rather than needing to be in motion. We get moments where everything is frozen but he's standing still, and he always seems to casually walk up to targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T00:20:53-08:00","id":1434909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1291628#post1291628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ki Rata's whole thing is that it's incredibly dangerous because it really is just the One Weird Trick that someone figured out that makes you win at fighting, right? It's h4x. It's like regular karate, like, not much more difficult to learn than regular karate, except if you learn it instead of learning karate, you can blow up cities. Whoops! Unfortunate that reality allows for such a thing, better police the hell out of the whole cosmos to ensure nobody spreads or exploits it!<br /> <br /> This doesn't really work in any system that assumes equal XP expenditures will lead to somewhat balanced characters. Which, like, I know, I know, <i>Exalted</i>, linear BP/exponential XP, feel free to laugh. But it's still a problem. You can't make a &quot;balanced&quot; version of Ki Rata because there isn't anything to Ki Rata except how unbalanced it is. Being phenomenally, existentially imbalanced is what Ki Rata <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> (Ironically it'd be easy to do in Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine because.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just about to say: Exalted's martial arts in general tend to be too...extra, for lack of a better word, to emulate Ki Rata. But Aspect from Nobilis/Glitch (or as Chuubo calls it, The Ace)? THAT is what you want: Sublime skill and absolute bodily control with pinpoint precision, plus a lot of &quot;I do this very specific, cool thing by hitting hard enough/in a certain way&quot;. At the moment 3e Solar Brawl seems a bit...not really focused on the pressure points Ki Rata implements, but I think you might have been able to approximate something with 2e's Solar Hero Style? Especially Solar Hero Supremacy. Ki Rata really feels like it fits more in the Celestial tier of martial arts than the Sidereal one. <br /> <br /> Also, Knave of Hearts gang reporting in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T00:32:19-08:00","id":1434912,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434890#post1434890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Unless Abandon has explicitly said something,</b> I don't believe he's literally stopping time. He's just moving so fast that for all appearances it looks like time has stopped. Ki Rata has been about being so fast and strong that the opponent has no chance. I don't see it going to literally warping the fabric of spacetime is a result of the style.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I also believe it's part of it,<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/724286011445739521/808615792177709066/unknown.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Organ Boy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434909#post1434909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ki Rata really feels like it fits more in the Celestial tier of martial arts than the Sidereal one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best way to describe it is Celestial design principles with Sidereal level of raw power. It doesn't, largely, do the weird esoteric stuff Sidereal styles are renowned for, but vastly outstrips Celestial styles in capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434885#post1434885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Brawl does not often break the action economy... but neither does Ki Rata that we have seen? Many Charms in Exalted are fluffed precisely like Ki Rata is - Solomon David's ability to just turn a group of people to blood sprays in the span of a single second may as well be represented by a charm that strikes several enemies around you and is just fluffed like you moved fast and hit them all individually (as several multi-target charms are);</div> </div> </div> </div>As Solomon demonstrates above, his multi-hit techniques aren't limited to hitting many different people or devastating battlegroups, he can strike one target many individual times, and that breaks action economy. For a more play-friendly Ki Rata, as I said previously, you can emulate such techniques via cribbing from capstones of Mantis and Centipede \u2014 but that would be a qualitative nerf and arguably remove the core conceit of Ki Rata's multi-hits as a style.<br /> <br /> So like, yes, we could nerf it enough for it to be applicable in play, and maybe that would be acceptable for non-Exalted and Terrestrial-medium practitioners of the style, true. But Ki Rata practiced on the Mastery (Solar/Sidereal) level would either lose the core thing which makes it unique, or become vastly less powerful than described.<br /> <br /> In short, my point is that Ki Rata as described in the comic, on the tabletop should <b>actually </b>let you launch 10k decisive attacks as one of it capstones before resetting you to base initiative, not just fluff-stunt that you're doing so. This is obviously unreasonably imbalanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","user":"Altasaire","date":". 02-09-2021, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T03:58:53-08:00","id":1434920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1434883#post1434883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being permissive enough of what counted as people being in line of sight and presuming an accessible vantage point from which to view all of Creation weren't exactly mechanics problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't really need to literally go slaying creation-wide for it to be problematic. Even assuming more stringent limits of what constitutes line of sight and eye range (like existence of the &quot;draw distance&quot;, inability to climb Mt Meru, and not allowing any form of rentgen vision) still left it with a number of issues.<br /> <br /> I mean, i know it wasn't the most problematic SMA out there, not by a wide margin, but that was only because few other styles were broken beyond reason.<br /> <br /> Still, getting back to the topic, Grandmother Spider Mastery is exactly what the &quot;mass hit&quot; ability of Ki Rata might look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T18:28:02-08:00","id":1435928,"title":"","content":"Edit: Wrong response","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T12:44:34-08:00","id":1436062,"title":"","content":"So, last few updates have made it clear that apparently Solomon isn't literally stopping time. Mottom was able to use magic to magic up a weapon for him to start using while he was in the middle of punching the hell out of someone in 'stopped time' so he is just moving so fast that he might as well be stopping time. Which is just slightly less hax then literally stopping time. Also, link only instead of image because of Mottom's kind of NSFW side boob<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/BOI31.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/BOI31.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/BOI31.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/BOI31.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-19-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T21:20:21-08:00","id":1436144,"title":"","content":"The basic principle of \u201cConcentrate lots of essence into a pinprick\u201d is premium Exalted martial arts material, the question is what that should <i>do</i> in terms of how to wring ten Charms out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T00:20:49-08:00","id":1436649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1436144#post1436144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic principle of \u201cConcentrate lots of essence into a pinprick\u201d is premium Exalted martial arts material, the question is what that should <i>do</i> in terms of how to wring ten Charms out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I have opinions about this, but decided to format them in the form of homebrew rather than trying to make a post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14hOzQsX2uKk7M0tICCOAGmjKzALv3tkxjiAk5xQwDlg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Clear Breaths of Annihilation, A Sidereal Martial Arts Style</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T13:54:44-08:00","id":1437145,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. I love Kill Six Billion Demons and love Ki Rata; but like SLS said I don't think it really fits with the milieu of Exalted Martial Arts of any kind. It's not really a job or an archetype or a concept; it's just a way of channeling essence that's BIGGER and STRONGER than all the others.<br /> <br /> That's... not what Martial Arts do in Exalted. In Exalted they gotta be balanced around one another. So even though each has its own niche you can't certify that one is absolutely better than another.<br /> <br /> Which, is basically the only thing we know about Ki Rata from the fiction. You could more closely emulate it with a selection of Solar Brawl, Integrity, and Resistance charms turned up so far as to break off the knob. You could certainly make a Brawl Supernal Solar Solomon David in Exalted, and give him a Martial Arts tree that mostly steals evocations from Gnomon; but he's not going to be destroying cities in one blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 03-01-2021, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T11:33:03-08:00","id":1437664,"title":"","content":"As people have noted, Ki Rata's whole thing is that it's broke, and the <i>lore</i> of it doesn't lead in a straightforward way to the <i>aesthetic</i> of it, but if you just want a style that captures the general aesthetic of Ki Rata, Charcoal March of Spiders with the poison and shaping bits taken out, and the thread gimmicks replaced with air shockwaves or something, isn't too far off. Of course we don't have a 3e CMoS, but I mean I think that &quot;what you'd do if you were homebrewing 3e CMos&quot; will get you in the ballpark.<br /> <br /> All that said, if I were actually going to design a PC-tier Ki Rata meant to be balanced against other styles, I'd probably draw inspiration from Snake Style -- the idea of being incredibly powerful but needing to maintain your discipline or else you become vulnerable or your powers go haywire feels a lot like Snake's &quot;always have tons of Initiative&quot; deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T23:23:53-08:00","id":1437764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288548-how-do-i-make-ki-rata?p=1436649#post1436649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I have opinions about this, but decided to format them in the form of homebrew rather than trying to make a post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14hOzQsX2uKk7M0tICCOAGmjKzALv3tkxjiAk5xQwDlg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Clear Breaths of Annihilation, A Sidereal Martial Arts Style</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no this basically covers everything Ki Rata is without being 'the boring best martial art ever.' It's stupidly destructive, and the kind of thing you would want to strictly regulate the use of. I think this is it. I especially love that it keeps Ki Rata's thing of being based around a breathing technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}